Implement per-app daily time limits in this iOS app, following the attached spec exactly. The spec is at <PATH_TO_SPEC.md>. Read it fully before writing a line. It is self-contained and was adversarially verified against this source. Do not re-derive its architecture conclusions. I am also giving you the UI mockups (image + HTML/CSS); they are the visual authority for wave 5 only.

Read CLAUDE.md first. It is the authoritative repository guidance and AGENTS.md symlinks to it.

Implement ALL SIX WAVES from the spec's §17 in one session, in order, without stopping for my approval between them. But gate every wave internally: after each wave, build the three schemes from CLAUDE.md sequentially, run the full test suite on the iPhone 17 simulator by ID, and run the invariant greps below. If ANY wave's gate fails and you cannot fix it within three attempts, STOP immediately, report exactly where you are, and do not proceed to the next wave. Never carry a red gate forward.

HARD RULES, non-negotiable:

1. Branch: I am on `ui-changes`. Confirm it and stop if it is anything else. Do not create, switch, or rename branches. The working tree already has unrelated badge and UI work; preserve it, never revert or clean it.
2. Never commit. I own all commits.
3. Test conventions per CLAUDE.md: pure XCTest, Foundation-only, no @testable import, ScreenTimeTests auto-compiles, production Shared files need hand-added per-target Sources-phase membership.

THE THREE THINGS THAT MUST NEVER HAPPEN. If you are about to do any of these, stop and tell me instead:

A. The threshold callback must NEVER write to ManagedSettingsStore. It writes a fact to the day-state file, then calls reconcileShields. After EVERY wave, grep: `ManagedSettingsStore(` must appear at exactly the two existing writer sites named in the spec's §4, and nowhere else.

B. NEVER call `DeviceActivityCenter.stopMonitoring()` with no arguments. Always pass the explicit activity-name array. The bare call would unregister the app's real block schedules.

C. Limits must never enter the effective-time pipeline. After EVERY wave, grep for new references to `appendActiveBlockSessionIfMissing`, `finalizeBlockSession`, `upsertFinalizedOccurrence` (there must be zero), and confirm zero edits to the spec's §7 do-not-touch file list.

ALSO:
- All Screen Time framework code is gated `#if !targetEnvironment(simulator)`. New DeviceActivity, ManagedSettings, and FamilyControls code must follow the same gating or the UIOnly scheme and tests break.
- Never call reconcileShields from inside a mutateLimitDayState closure. Mutate completes, then reconcile. The locks must never nest (§6).
- `includesPastActivity: true` on every event, always. `false` makes limits gameable by any config edit.
- Suppress the warning callback for allowances of 5 minutes or less. Measured on device: iOS fires it instantly at interval start for those.
- No screen may show a countdown, a progress bar, or "X of Y minutes used". iOS provides no usage-read API. Three states only: ACTIVE, WARNING FIRED, REACHED.

WAVE 3 IS THE ONE TO GET RIGHT. Its test requires that with an empty limitApps set, the shield planner produces byte-identical output to today, and every existing planner test passes UNMODIFIED. If you have to change an existing planner test to make it pass, you have broken something. Stop and tell me.

FIRST, BEFORE ANY CODE: the spec's §0 flags a working-tree anomaly. An untracked `ScreenTime/Sources/Probe/` folder exists but is wired into nothing; its hook edits were reverted. Verify the current state, report what you find, and confirm the DeviceActivityMonitor has no `eventDidReachThreshold` override at HEAD. Do not restore or delete the probe. Write the new production overrides so a DEBUG probe early-return can be re-inserted at the top later without conflict.

Then run all six waves. For wave 5, use XcodeBuildMCP to boot the simulator and screenshot each screen against the mockups; verify visually, do not assume.

Report, per wave: what you built, the gate result, and the grep results for A and C. At the end, give me the device-verify checklist from the spec's §15, since the simulator cannot exercise the Screen Time path. Then stop.[Image #1] [Image #2] [Image #3] [Image #4] [Image #5] [Image #6] [Image #7] [Image #8] [Image #9] <!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Nudge — Time Limits</title>
<style>
:root{
  --bg:#000;--card:#151517;--card2:#202024;--stroke:rgba(255,255,255,.07);
  --txt:#F5F5F7;--txt2:#98989F;--txt3:#5B5B63;
  --acc:#8B9DFF;--acc-deep:#5E70E8;--mint:#5FD4A8;--amber:#F2B95C;--rose:#F07A7A;
}
*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased}
body{background:#0A0A0C;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"SF Pro Display","SF Pro Text",Inter,sans-serif;color:var(--txt);padding:64px 40px}
h1{font-size:22px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.3px;text-align:center;margin:72px 0 8px}
h1:first-of-type{margin-top:0}
.note{max-width:640px;margin:0 auto 28px;text-align:center;font-size:13px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--txt2)}
.row{display:flex;gap:36px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;align-items:flex-start}
.unit{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center}
.label{text-align:center;color:var(--txt3);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-top:12px}
.panel{width:393px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:36px;padding:22px 20px;box-shadow:0 20px 50px rgba(0,0,0,.5)}
.eyebrow{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--txt3);display:block;margin-bottom:12px}
.card{background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--stroke);border-radius:24px;padding:2px 16px}
.chev{color:var(--txt3);margin-left:auto;font-size:17px;flex:none}

/* app tiles */
.app{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:9px;flex:none;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;color:#fff}
.a-yt{background:#E53935}
.a-ig{background:linear-gradient(45deg,#FEDA75,#D62976,#4F5BD5)}
.a-tt{background:#111;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #333}
.a-x{background:#26262B;box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px #3A3A40}
.a-hk{background:#3B4CC8}
.a-rd{background:#FF4500}

/* ============ 1. LIMITS SECTION ============ */
.lrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:13px 0}
.lrow + .lrow{border-top:1px solid var(--stroke)}
.lrow .m{flex:1;min-width:0}
.lrow .t{font-size:15px;font-weight:700;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.lrow .s{font-size:12px;color:var(--txt2);margin-top:3px;font-weight:600}
.state{flex:none;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
.ring-o{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;border:2px solid #3E3E45}
.warnpill{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;background:rgba(242,185,92,.12);border-radius:100px;padding:4px 9px;font-size:11px;font-weight:800;color:var(--amber)}
.warnpill i{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--amber)}
.donechk{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:rgba(139,157,255,.22);color:var(--acc);display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:9px;font-weight:900}
.lrow.done .app{opacity:.45}
.lrow.done .t{color:var(--txt2)}
.lrow.done .s{color:var(--txt3)}
.newrow{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:13px 0;color:var(--acc);font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700}
.newtile{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(139,157,255,.1);display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:16px;flex:none}
.blockmini{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:13px 0}
.blockmini + .blockmini{border-top:1px solid var(--stroke)}
.bico{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:9px;background:rgba(139,157,255,.14);display:grid;place-items:center;color:var(--acc);flex:none}
.blockmini .t{font-size:15px;font-weight:700}
.blockmini .s{font-size:12px;color:var(--txt2);margin-top:3px}
.empty{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;text-align:center;padding:26px 20px 22px}
.empty .glyph{width:52px;height:52px;border-radius:16px;background:var(--card2);display:grid;place-items:center;margin-bottom:14px}
.empty .glyph svg{width:24px;height:24px;stroke:var(--txt3);fill:none;stroke-width:1.8;stroke-linecap:round}
.empty .t{font-size:15px;font-weight:700}
.empty .s{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--txt2);margin-top:5px;line-height:1.45}
.empty .btn{margin-top:16px;background:rgba(139,157,255,.14);color:var(--acc);border-radius:100px;padding:9px 18px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:800}

/* ============ 2. CREATE ============ */
.sheet{background:#161619;border-radius:30px;padding:12px 18px 18px;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}
.grab{width:38px;height:5px;border-radius:3px;background:#3A3A40;margin:0 auto}
.shead{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between}
.shead .c{font-size:15px;color:var(--txt2);font-weight:600}
.shead .t{font-size:16px;font-weight:800}
.field{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--stroke);border-radius:18px;padding:13px 15px}
.field .ph{font-size:14.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--txt3);flex:1}
.field .sel{font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700;flex:1}
.field .dash{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:9px;border:1.5px dashed #3A3A40;flex:none}
.durgrid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:8px}
.dchip{background:var(--card);border:1.5px solid var(--stroke);border-radius:14px;padding:12px 0;text-align:center;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt2)}
.dchip.on{border-color:var(--acc);background:rgba(139,157,255,.1);color:var(--txt)}
.savebtn{border-radius:18px;padding:15px;text-align:center;font-size:16px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.2px}
.savebtn.off{background:var(--card2);color:var(--txt3)}
.savebtn.on{background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--acc),var(--acc-deep));color:#0B0D1A;box-shadow:0 8px 24px rgba(94,112,232,.35)}
.finehint{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--txt3);text-align:center;font-weight:600}

/* ============ 3. DETAIL ============ */
.dhero{text-align:center;padding:8px 0 2px}
.dhero .app{width:64px;height:64px;border-radius:18px;margin:0 auto;font-size:26px}
.dhero .t{font-size:21px;font-weight:800;margin-top:12px;letter-spacing:-.3px}
.dhero .s{font-size:13px;color:var(--txt2);font-weight:600;margin-top:4px}
.statecard{display:flex;gap:13px;align-items:flex-start;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--stroke);border-radius:20px;padding:15px 16px}
.statecard .si{flex:none;margin-top:1px}
.statecard .t{font-size:14.5px;font-weight:700}
.statecard .s{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--txt2);margin-top:4px;line-height:1.45}
.statecard.reached{border-color:rgba(139,157,255,.25)}
.opt{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:13px 0;font-size:15px;font-weight:700}
.opt + .opt{border-top:1px solid var(--stroke)}
.oico{width:30px;height:30px;border-radius:9px;display:grid;place-items:center;font-size:13px;flex:none}
.opt.danger{color:var(--rose)}
.opt.unlock{color:var(--acc)}

/* ============ 4. SHIELD ============ */
.shield{width:393px;height:700px;background:var(--bg);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.09);border-radius:44px;box-shadow:0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,.6);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:40px 34px;gap:0}
.shield .app{width:72px;height:72px;border-radius:20px;font-size:30px}
.shield h3{font-size:26px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.5px;margin-top:26px;line-height:1.25}
.shield p{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--txt2);line-height:1.55;margin-top:12px;max-width:280px}
.shield .midnight{margin-top:22px;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--stroke);border-radius:100px;padding:9px 16px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt2)}
.shield .midnight i{width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--acc);display:block}
.shield .done{margin-top:auto;width:100%;background:#fff;color:#000;border-radius:18px;padding:15px;font-size:16px;font-weight:800}
.shield .hatch{margin-top:14px;font-size:13px;font-weight:700;color:var(--txt3)}
.shield .hatch b{color:var(--txt2);text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px;font-weight:700}

/* ============ 5/6. NOTIFICATIONS ============ */
.notif{width:380px;background:rgba(32,32,36,.96);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);border-radius:22px;padding:13px 14px;display:flex;gap:11px;align-items:flex-start;box-shadow:0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,.5)}
.notif .app{width:36px;height:36px;border-radius:9px;font-size:15px}
.notif .m{flex:1}
.notif .h{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline}
.notif .t{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700}
.notif .when{font-size:11px;color:var(--txt3);font-weight:600}
.notif .b{font-size:13px;color:var(--txt2);margin-top:3px;line-height:1.4}
.nstack{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;align-items:center}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- ================= 1. LIMITS SECTION ================= -->
<h1>1 · Limits on the Block List tab</h1>
<div class="row">

<div class="unit">
<div class="panel">
  <span class="eyebrow">Blocks</span>
  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:20px">
    <div class="blockmini"><div class="bico"><svg width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l8 3v6c0 5-3.4 9.4-8 11-4.6-1.6-8-6-8-11V5z"/></svg></div><div style="flex:1"><div class="t">Deep Work</div><div class="s">9:00 – 11:00 PM · Weekdays</div></div><span class="chev">›</span></div>
    <div class="blockmini"><div class="bico"><svg width="16" height="16" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 2l8 3v6c0 5-3.4 9.4-8 11-4.6-1.6-8-6-8-11V5z"/></svg></div><div style="flex:1"><div class="t">Wind-down</div><div class="s">11:11 – 11:50 PM · Weekdays</div></div><span class="chev">›</span></div>
  </div>

  <span class="eyebrow">Daily limits</span>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="lrow">
      <div class="app a-yt">▶</div>
      <div class="m"><div class="t">YouTube</div><div class="s">30m a day</div></div>
      <span class="state"><span class="ring-o"></span></span>
      <span class="chev">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <div class="app a-ig">📷</div>
      <div class="m"><div class="t">Instagram</div><div class="s">20m a day</div></div>
      <span class="state"><span class="warnpill"><i></i>5m warning · 2:14 PM</span></span>
      <span class="chev">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lrow done">
      <div class="app a-tt">♪</div>
      <div class="m"><div class="t">TikTok</div><div class="s">Done · back at midnight</div></div>
      <span class="state"><span class="donechk">✓</span></span>
      <span class="chev">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lrow">
      <div class="app a-hk">星</div>
      <div class="m"><div class="t">Honkai: Star Rail — Interstellar Edition</div><div class="s">45m a day</div></div>
      <span class="state"><span class="ring-o"></span></span>
      <span class="chev">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="lrow done">
      <div class="app a-x">𝕏</div>
      <div class="m"><div class="t">X</div><div class="s">Done · back at midnight</div></div>
      <span class="state"><span class="donechk">✓</span></span>
      <span class="chev">›</span>
    </div>
    <div class="newrow"><div class="newtile">＋</div>New limit</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="label">Section · all three states</div>
</div>

<div class="unit">
<div class="panel">
  <span class="eyebrow">Daily limits</span>
  <div class="card empty">
    <div class="glyph"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6 2h12M6 22h12M7 2c0 5 4 6 5 8-1 2-5 3-5 8M17 2c0 5-4 6-5 8 1 2 5 3 5 8"/></svg></div>
    <div class="t">No daily limits yet</div>
    <div class="s">Give an app a daily allowance.<br>When it's used up, the app rests until midnight.</div>
    <div class="btn">＋ New limit</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="label">Empty state</div>
</div>

</div>
<p class="note">Honest "not reached yet" = a hollow ring: the day is open, nothing more is knowable, so nothing more is shown. The warning moment is the only specific fact the app ever learns, so the row records it as a timestamped amber pill ("5m warning · 2:14 PM") rather than a live countdown that would immediately drift wrong. Reached rows keep their place but read as settled: dimmed icon, filled periwinkle check, "Done · back at midnight". Same row anatomy as Blocks, separate eyebrow, so the two sections are siblings, not rivals.</p>

<!-- ================= 2. CREATE ================= -->
<h1>2 · Create a limit</h1>
<div class="row">

<div class="unit">
<div class="panel"><div class="sheet">
  <div class="grab"></div>
  <div class="shead"><span class="c">Cancel</span><span class="t">New Limit</span><span style="width:44px"></span></div>
  <div class="field"><div class="dash"></div><span class="ph">Choose an app</span><span class="chev">›</span></div>
  <span class="eyebrow" style="margin:2px 0 0">Daily allowance</span>
  <div class="durgrid">
    <div class="dchip">15m</div><div class="dchip">30m</div><div class="dchip">45m</div>
    <div class="dchip">1h</div><div class="dchip">2h</div><div class="dchip">Custom</div>
  </div>
  <div class="savebtn off">Set Limit</div>
</div></div>
<div class="label">Nothing chosen · save disabled</div>
</div>

<div class="unit">
<div class="panel"><div class="sheet">
  <div class="grab"></div>
  <div class="shead"><span class="c">Cancel</span><span class="t">New Limit</span><span style="width:44px"></span></div>
  <div class="field"><div class="app a-yt">▶</div><span class="sel">YouTube</span><span class="chev">›</span></div>
  <span class="eyebrow" style="margin:2px 0 0">Daily allowance</span>
  <div class="durgrid">
    <div class="dchip">15m</div><div class="dchip on">30m</div><div class="dchip">45m</div>
    <div class="dchip">1h</div><div class="dchip">2h</div><div class="dchip">Custom</div>
  </div>
  <div class="savebtn on">Set Limit · 30m a day</div>
  <div class="finehint">Resets every night at midnight</div>
</div></div>
<div class="label">Ready · save enabled</div>
</div>

</div>
<p class="note">Two decisions only: which app, how long. Six preset chips cover almost everyone; Custom opens a wheel. The save button repeats the choice back ("Set Limit · 30m a day") so confirmation doubles as a summary, and the reset rule is one quiet line under the button, taught at the moment it matters.</p>

<!-- ================= 3. DETAIL ================= -->
<h1>3 · Limit detail</h1>
<div class="row">

<div class="unit">
<div class="panel" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
  <div class="dhero">
    <div class="app a-yt">▶</div>
    <div class="t">YouTube</div>
    <div class="s">30 minutes a day</div>
  </div>
  <div class="statecard">
    <span class="si ring-o" style="width:18px;height:18px"></span>
    <div><div class="t">Running today</div><div class="s">iOS doesn't share running totals. You'll get a heads-up when 5 minutes remain.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="opt"><div class="oico" style="background:rgba(139,157,255,.12);color:var(--acc)">✎</div>Edit allowance<span class="chev" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--txt2);margin-left:auto">30m ›</span></div>
    <div class="opt"><div class="oico" style="background:rgba(242,185,92,.12);color:var(--amber)">⏸</div>Skip today<span class="chev">›</span></div>
    <div class="opt danger"><div class="oico" style="background:rgba(240,122,122,.12);color:var(--rose)">🗑</div>Delete limit</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="label">Active state</div>
</div>

<div class="unit">
<div class="panel" style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px">
  <div class="dhero">
    <div class="app a-yt" style="opacity:.5">▶</div>
    <div class="t" style="color:var(--txt2)">YouTube</div>
    <div class="s">30 minutes a day</div>
  </div>
  <div class="statecard reached">
    <span class="si donechk" style="width:18px;height:18px;font-size:10px">✓</span>
    <div><div class="t">Done for today</div><div class="s">Reached at 2:19 PM. YouTube is shielded until midnight, then your 30 minutes are back.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="opt unlock"><div class="oico" style="background:rgba(139,157,255,.12);color:var(--acc)">🔓</div>Unlock for today</div>
    <div class="opt"><div class="oico" style="background:rgba(139,157,255,.12);color:var(--acc)">✎</div>Edit allowance<span class="chev" style="font-size:13px;color:var(--txt2);margin-left:auto">30m ›</span></div>
    <div class="opt danger"><div class="oico" style="background:rgba(240,122,122,.12);color:var(--rose)">🗑</div>Delete limit</div>
  </div>
</div>
<div class="label">Reached state</div>
</div>

</div>
<p class="note">Active says the honest thing out loud: totals aren't knowable, the warning is the deal. Reached shows the one fact the app does know, the shield timestamp, and swaps "Skip today" for "Unlock for today" since skipping no longer means anything. The dimmed hero mirrors the row treatment so the two screens agree.</p>

<!-- ================= 4. SHIELD ================= -->
<h1>4 · The limit shield</h1>
<div class="row">

<div class="unit">
<div class="shield">
  <div class="app a-yt">▶</div>
  <h3>That's your<br>30 minutes.</h3>
  <p>You gave YouTube half an hour a day. Today's half hour is spent.</p>
  <div class="midnight"><i></i>Opens again at 12:00 AM</div>
  <div class="done">Done for today</div>
</div>
<div class="label">No escape hatch</div>
</div>

<div class="unit">
<div class="shield">
  <div class="app a-yt">▶</div>
  <h3>That's your<br>30 minutes.</h3>
  <p>You gave YouTube half an hour a day. Today's half hour is spent.</p>
  <div class="midnight"><i></i>Opens again at 12:00 AM</div>
  <div class="done">Done for today</div>
  <div class="hatch">Really need it? <b>Unlock for today</b></div>
</div>
<div class="label">With escape hatch</div>
</div>

</div>
<p class="note">Second person, past tense, the user's own rule quoted back: "you gave YouTube half an hour". The primary action is leaving, styled as completion ("Done for today"), never "OK" like an error. The hatch version buries the unlock as small tertiary text with a question in front of it, one breath of friction, and it unlocks the whole day rather than adding minutes, because minutes can't be counted.</p>

<!-- ================= 5. WARNING NOTIFICATION ================= -->
<h1>5 · The 5-minute warning</h1>
<div class="nstack">
  <div class="notif"><div class="app a-yt">▶</div><div class="m"><div class="h"><span class="t">Nudge</span><span class="when">now</span></div><div class="b">5 minutes left on YouTube today.</div></div></div>
  <div class="notif"><div class="app a-yt">▶</div><div class="m"><div class="h"><span class="t">Nudge</span><span class="when">now</span></div><div class="b">Last 5 YouTube minutes. Make them good ones.</div></div></div>
  <div class="notif"><div class="app a-yt">▶</div><div class="m"><div class="h"><span class="t">Nudge</span><span class="when">now</span></div><div class="b">YouTube wraps up in 5 minutes. Good place to land the plane.</div></div></div>
</div>
<p class="note">Top: neutral, pure information. Middle: warm nudge, treats the remaining time as valuable rather than threatened. Bottom: coach voice with a concrete suggestion. All three state the only fact known: 5 minutes, right now.</p>

<!-- ================= 6. REACHED NOTIFICATION ================= -->
<h1>6 · Limit reached</h1>
<div class="nstack">
  <div class="notif"><div class="app a-yt">▶</div><div class="m"><div class="h"><span class="t">Nudge</span><span class="when">now</span></div><div class="b">That's 30 minutes of YouTube. Shielded until midnight.</div></div></div>
  <div class="notif"><div class="app a-yt">▶</div><div class="m"><div class="h"><span class="t">Nudge</span><span class="when">now</span></div><div class="b">YouTube is done for today. Your evening's yours back.</div></div></div>
</div>
<p class="note">Both close the loop without judgment: first restates the user's own number, second reframes the shield as a gain. Neither says "blocked" or "limit exceeded", the user didn't fail, the plan worked.</p>

